          %h3#relation_to_schurs_lemma Relation to Schur’s lemma
          %p
            The (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"}> isomorphism classes
            ) of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representations"} irreducible representations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i
            form the canonical
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} linear basis
            of the representation ring:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  R(G) \;\simeq\; \mathbb{Z}\big[  \{V_i\}_i \big]
                  \\,.
          %p
            Moreover, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            assigning
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimensions"} dimensions
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            constitutes a canonical bilinear symmetric
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+product"} inner product
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\langle -,-\rangle
                  \\;\colon\;
                  R(G) \times R(G)
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbb{Z}
                  \\,.
          %p
            In terms of this,
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schur%27s+lemma"} Schur's lemma
            states that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representations"} irreducible representations
            generally constitute an
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+basis"} orthogonal basis
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthonormal+basis"} orthonormal basis
            when the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed
          %p For more discussion of this perspective, see
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                at
                %em
